# * print --export: reproduce the whole journal

# ** 1. Directives, top-level comment lines and comment blocks are reproduced verbatim,
# in the original order, with transactions rendered as print normally renders them.
# Blank lines are normalised: one between transactions and between groups of directive/comment lines.
# Comment lines immediately preceding a transaction stay with it.
# A ! or @ directive prefix is dropped. apply account, alias, their end forms, and Ledger directives
# which hledger ignores (like assert) are not reproduced; their effects are already applied.
<
; top comment
# hash comment
* org heading

account assets:cash  ; type:A
  ; a subdirective comment
!account expenses:food
commodity $1,000.00
commodity EUR
  format 1.000,00 EUR
D $1,000.00
decimal-mark .
payee Foo  ; some payee
tag mytag
P 2024-01-01 EUR $1.10
~ monthly  forecast
    (assets:cash)  10
= expenses:food
    (expenses:food:auto)  *0.1
alias food = expenses:food
apply account top
assert foo
2024-01-02 * (123) Foo  ; txn comment
    ; another txn comment line
    food   $5  ; posting comment
    assets:cash

end apply account
end aliases
comment
a comment block
end comment

; preceding comment 1
; preceding comment 2
2024-01-03 later
    assets:cash  $-1
    expenses:food

2024-01-01 earlier
    assets:cash  1
    expenses:food
; trailing comment
$ hledger -f - print --export
; top comment
# hash comment
* org heading

account assets:cash  ; type:A
  ; a subdirective comment
account expenses:food
commodity $1,000.00
commodity EUR
  format 1.000,00 EUR
D $1,000.00
decimal-mark .
payee Foo  ; some payee
tag mytag
P 2024-01-01 EUR $1.10
~ monthly  forecast
    (assets:cash)  10
= expenses:food
    (expenses:food:auto)  *0.1

2024-01-02 * (123) Foo  ; txn comment
    ; another txn comment line
    top:food                                      $5  ; posting comment
    top:assets:cash

comment
a comment block
end comment

; preceding comment 1
; preceding comment 2
2024-01-03 later
    assets:cash                                  $-1
    expenses:food

2024-01-01 earlier
    assets:cash                                   $1.00
    expenses:food

; trailing comment
>= 0

# ** 2. A query selects the transactions shown, but all directives and comments are kept.
<
account a

; before 1
2024-01-01 one
    (a)  1

; before 2
2024-01-02 two
    (a)  2
$ hledger -f - print --export date:2024-01-02
account a

; before 2
2024-01-02 two
    (a)                                            2

>= 0

# ** 3. Transactions generated by --forecast, and postings generated by --auto, are not shown.
<
~ monthly from 2024-02  forecast
    (a)  10

= a
    (b)  *2

2024-01-01 one
    (a)  1
$ hledger -f - print --export --forecast=2024-02..2024-04 --auto
~ monthly from 2024-02  forecast
    (a)  10

= a
    (b)  *2

2024-01-01 one
    (a)                                            1

>= 0

# ** 4. Included files are inlined in place of the include directive.
$ hledger -f export-main.j print --export
; export-main.j: a journal with an include
Y 2024

# export-included.j

2024-01-02 included txn
    (inc:b)                                        2

; after the include
2024-01-03 main txn
    (a)                                            3

>= 0

# ** 5. A file included twice is reproduced twice. Transactions from a non-journal file
# (eg an included CSV file) are added at the end.
$ hledger -f export-main2.j print --export
; export-main2.j: includes a csv file, and a journal file twice
# export-included.j

2024-01-02 included txn
    (inc:b)                                        2

# export-included.j

2024-01-02 included txn
    (inc:b)                                        2

2024-01-06 last
    (a)                                            6

2024-01-05 csv txn
    c                                              5
    income:unknown                                -5

>= 0

# ** 6. With a non-journal main file, just the transactions are shown, in file order.
$ hledger -f export-inc.csv print --export
2024-01-05 csv txn
    c                                              5
    income:unknown                                -5

>= 0

# ** 7. Only the txt output format is supported.
$ hledger -f export-main.j print --export -O csv
>2 /print --export supports only the txt output format/
>= 1
